[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How the rows are covered
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is covered by a differential test that constructs the trigger, calls
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m BOTH `.so`s, and asserts the **same error code** via
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `ZSTD_getErrorCode`/`FSE_isError`/`HUF_isError`/`ZDICT_isError` — not merely
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "both failed". The `test` column names the covering test.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows fall into two coverage kinds:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **direct** — the test hands the exact invalid argument to the exact public
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   entry point (rows 1–99 below, plus every `parameter_outOfBound` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `parameter_unsupported` / `stage_wrong` / `dstSize_tooSmall` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `srcSize_wrong` / `memory_allocation` / `workSpace_tooSmall` /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `dictionary_*` / `stabilityCondition_notRespected` site).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **constructive-corruption** — for the deep bitstream/entropy checks
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (`corruption_detected`, `tableLog_tooLarge`, `maxSymbolValue_too*`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `checksum_wrong`, `literals_headerWrong`, `dictionary_corrupted` inside
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   entropy loading, and every legacy-decoder check) the test constructs the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   invalid condition by systematically mutating valid frames/headers/tables:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `c4_corruption.rs` performs an **exhaustive single-byte sweep** (every byte
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   offset × every one of the 8 bit flips, plus 0x00/0xFF stamping) over frames
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   produced in all of the `CONFIGS.md` configurations, plus every truncation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   length, plus random-garbage buffers, and asserts C and Rust return the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   identical error code (or the identical success) for *each* mutation. That
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   drives these sites with the exact conditions they test, and — critically —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   asserts equality on the whole reachable error lattice rather than one point
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   in it.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
