use std::os::raw::{c_int, c_uint, c_void};

FIRST run `nm -D --defined-only c_src/build/libzstd.so | grep -E ' (ZBUFF|ZSTDv0|ZBUFFv0|FSEv0|HUFv0)'` to get the exact exported symbol list and cover EVERY one of them across the three files. Read the matching legacy headers/sources for EXACT signatures - a wrong signature causes segfaults. Use has_both(name) to gate anything you are unsure about, but do NOT gate away symbols that ARE exported (that would make the test vacuous).

HOW TO GET LEGACY TEST INPUT: you cannot produce legacy frames with the current encoder. Instead:
(a) Synthesize buffers that START with each legacy magic number - read the exact magic constants out of the legacy C sources/headers (do not trust guesses) - followed by random and structured payloads.
(b) Exhaustively sweep single-byte mutations of those buffers, every truncation length from 0 to N, and thousands of random-garbage buffers with a FIXED seed.
The POINT: C and Rust must return the IDENTICAL result/error code for every such input. Compare error codes with the version's own ZSTDv0x_isError plus ZSTDv0x_getErrorName, comparing BOTH the boolean and the STRING - not just 'both failed'.
Also: feed valid MODERN frames (produce them with ZSTD_compress from each .so) to the legacy entry points, and feed legacy-magic buffers to ZSTD_decompress, ZSTD_getFrameContentSize, ZSTD_isFrame, ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize, ZSTD_decompressStream, ZSTD_getFrameHeader and assert identical results. Cover dst capacity sweeps {0,1,small,exact,large} and the streaming legacy entry points (createDCtx/freeDCtx/resetDCtx/decompressContinue/nextSrcSizeToDecompress and ZBUFFv0x_*) where exported.

c12_deprecated.rs (ZBUFF ERROR paths) must cover: compressContinue/compressFlush/compressEnd called without init; decompressContinue without init; dst capacity 0 and 1; corrupted and truncated input to ZBUFF_decompressContinue (exhaustive single-byte mutation sweep of a valid ZBUFF-produced stream); ZBUFF_compressInit with out-of-range compression levels (INT_MIN, -1000000, 0, 23, 100, INT_MAX); ZBUFF_compressInitDictionary / ZBUFF_decompressInitDictionary with NULL dict + nonzero size, a corrupted trained dictionary, and dictSize 0; and ZBUFF_getErrorName over every int from -200 to 400 (this covers out-of-range enum values with no valid variant). Compare BOTH the ZBUFF_isError boolean and the ZBUFF_getErrorName string in every case.

GLOBAL REQUIREMENTS:
- Every call must go through both::<T>("name"). NEVER call Rust functions directly.
- Fixed RNG seeds; MANY randomized inputs per case, not one hand-picked value.
- IMPORTANT: when using gen(shape, len, &mut rng) ALWAYS pass buf.len() (not len) as any size argument - Shape::Empty returns an empty Vec regardless of len; passing len causes out-of-bounds reads and SIGSEGV.
- Never pass a pointer from one library's context into the other library's functions.
- Keep each #[test] finishing well under 300 seconds; split into multiple #[test] functions.

VERIFY YOUR WORK: run `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --test c12_deprecated`, `--release --test b15_legacy`, `--release --test c13_legacy`. ALL must PASS. Also re-run `timeout 600 cargo test --release --test b14_deprecated` at the end to confirm you did not break it. If you find a genuine divergence, FIX THE RUST SOURCE under translation/src/ (the C is ground truth; NEVER modify c_src/), then `cargo build --release` and re-run until green.

